,"attempts":0,"answerDescription":"Answer format: ****************"}}],"type":"vm","title":"[Medium] [Scripting] Very Secure Protocol","taskNo":15,"created":"2019-10-25T18:22:47.326Z","deadline":null,"uploadId":"5db33b9bfffd3666d13c4a66","description":"<p>Get the protocol description <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_d-_g9dfCiFMJRyPVh-JPwIf9Kpozd7I/view?usp=sharing\">here</a></p><p>Just a few things to note when carrying out this challenge:</p><ul><li>you'll need to use the <a href=\"https://cryptography.io/en/latest/\">PyCA</a> library for the cryptographic components</li><li>the hashes and encrypted data are sent in bytes so need to be encoded correctly</li><li>The hashed PSK is 32 bytes. No password file has strings this long. If you find a password file(rockyou.txt), make sure the minimum length is 32 bytes(do this by copying the same string until it is 32 bytes). </li><li>The protocol is running on port 3000</li></ul><p>Once you receive the PRE-AUTH-CONF value, send it in every packet to the server!</p>","taskVmRegions":["eu-west-1"],"hasUploadOwnership":false}]}